SUMMARY:MTPL Book Discussion Group
DESCRIPTION:Start your Wednesday with a side of storytelling. The MTPL Book
  Discussion Group meets the 2nd Wednesday of each month at 10am to explore
  new worlds together. It’s more than just a book club—it’s your mont
 hly morning retreat for thoughtful talk and local connection. We’ve got 
 the books\; we just need you! Please register for each meeting\, as it all
 ows the library to update you if there are any changes to a meeting due to
  weather delays\, closures\, or other circumstances. January 14: 1984 by G
 eorge Orwell February 11: Empire of AI by Karen Hao March 11: The Greatest
  Generation by Tom Brokaw April 8: West with Giraffes by Lynda Rutledge Ma
 y 13: Klara and the Sun by Kazuo Ishiguro June 10: Everything is Tuberculo
 sis by John Green July 8: Kindred by Octavia Butler August 12: There Is No
  Place for Us by Brian Goldstone September 9: The Secret History by Donna 
 Tartt October 14: On Call by Anthony Fauci November 11: Harlem Shuffle by 
